<!-- The contradiction ledger for one subject, at contradictions/<subject_kind>/<slug>.md
     (Wiki/schema/entities.yaml → kinds.contradiction). Two trees: subject_kind concept is
     keyed by concept slug, subject_kind entity by a named entity, so one clash is reachable
     from both sides.

     Append-only. A recorded contradiction is never deleted or rewritten; when it is settled
     it moves from Open to Resolved with the resolution that settled it and stays there. That
     permanence is the point: a document arriving next year is checked against clashes found
     long before it, which a list of currently-open questions could not do.

     This file is evidence, never a verdict. It records that sources disagree; deciding which
     is right is /tetraframe and a D-xx, and the author's call. The concept page itself states
     only what the sources agree on and links here through contradiction_ref. -->

